<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31382" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nūgor</span></b> , ātus, 1,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i>
			[id.]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To jest, trifle, play the fool, talk nonsense</i> (
			= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλυαρεῖν</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syn. ludo): Democritus non inscite nugatur, ut
					physicus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 13, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum aliquo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 1, 73</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 2, 1,
			93</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To trick, cajole, cheat</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nugatur sciens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 5, 4, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non mihi nugari potes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Ep. 3, 4, 42</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Trin. 4, 2, 55</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
